[B][SIZE=6]Project Gielinor — Native Rust OSRS 239.1 Client[/SIZE][/B]

Hi everyone! Here is our native Rust OSRS 239.1 client, from early cache experiments to the current development build. It runs without a JVM. Client parity work continues.

Live captures use an isolated Kotlin reference server. Offline renders and test harnesses are labeled; these checkpoints do not establish complete parity.

[I]Live native client — Current checkpoint: native world, actors, inventory, chat and minimap.[/I]
[IMG]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/autismoyah-hub/project-gielinor-showcase/main/images/client-parity/01-current-native.png[/IMG]

[B][SIZE=4]From terrain experiments to a native world[/SIZE][/B]

Early steps: JS5, cache decoding and asset loading, before the scene and interface came together.

[I]Offline renderer test — Early terrain decoding: Lumbridge before the scene was assembled.[/I]
[IMG]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/autismoyah-hub/project-gielinor-showcase/main/images/client-parity/02-early-terrain.png[/IMG]

[I]Historical live native client — Early live viewport: scene loaded; minimap and interface work still ahead.[/I]
[IMG]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/autismoyah-hub/project-gielinor-showcase/main/images/client-parity/03-early-live.png[/IMG]

[B][SIZE=4]Login, protocol and audio[/SIZE][/B]

Native login, authentication and encrypted networking target revision 239.1. Packet tables match; broader protocol and session parity remain ongoing.

[I]Offline title test — Cached title artwork, fonts and animated fire.[/I]
[IMG]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/autismoyah-hub/project-gielinor-showcase/main/images/client-parity/04-title.png[/IMG]

[I]Controlled session test — Authenticator rejection and retry screen.[/I]
[IMG]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/autismoyah-hub/project-gielinor-showcase/main/images/client-parity/05-authenticator.png[/IMG]

Music, jingles and positional effects mix on an independent native audio worker. Token login has controlled coverage; real-issuer acceptance remains open.

